{"schema_version":"cera.scene_writer_draft.v1","story_text":"Hana smiled, the warmth of the hallway light catching the soft lines around her eyes. She gave a small, pleased nod, her hands folded loosely in front of her. \"It went really well,\" she said, her voice gentle and genuine. \"I'm glad you came.\"\n\nBehind her, Mia lingered near the coat rack, quiet and still, watching the exchange without stepping forward. The entryway felt snug, filled with the faint smell of cooking spices and the soft hum of the house settling around them.\n\nHana paused, letting her words hang in the air, leaving room for whatever Ted might say next."}